    "result_text": "The full build passes. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: `riskFlag` on owner responses\n\nThe spec: return `riskFlag` true when **any** of three softer signals hold \u2014 possible duplicate, disposable-adjacent email domain, or city over its soft capacity.\n\nEach condition already had a home in the domain, so I reused rather than duplicated, and kept the OR-combining logic in its own small class:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the new `riskFlag` boolean (read-only) on the `OwnerDto` schema, alongside the existing `bulkSignupWarning` / `capacityWarning` warnings. The DTO (and its `setRiskFlag`) is generated from this spec.\n\n2. **`DisposableEmailDomains`** \u2014 added `isAdjacent(email)` next to the existing `isBlocked(email)`, defining \"disposable-adjacent\" as *a subdomain of a blocked throwaway provider* (e.g. `inbox.mailinator.com`) \u2014 the near-miss that slips past the exact-match block that already rejects owners at create time. Factored out a shared `domainOf(...)` helper so both methods parse the domain the same way (single source of truth for the blocklist).\n\n3. **`RiskFlag`** (new) \u2014 a small package-private helper mirroring `CapacityWarning` / `PossibleDuplicate`, with one responsibility: combine the three signals \u2014 `possibleDuplicateOf != null`, `DisposableEmailDomains.isAdjacent(email)`, and `CapacityWarning.isRaised(city, repo)` (the existing 40-owner soft threshold below the hard cap of 50).\n\n4. **`OwnerResponses.toDto`** \u2014 stamps `riskFlag` onto every owner response (create/read/idempotent replay), exactly where the sibling warnings are stamped, so all owner representations stay identical.\n\nThe one new test (`coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`) and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
